From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 11:36:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep incremental layout from losing content

The `incremental` feature gates box construction on damage, so
resolve_layout_children only re-collects a node whose damage carries
CONSTRUCT_FC | CONSTRUCT_BOX. Everything that used to be rebuilt on
every pass now has to earn it, and several things silently stopped
happening.

A node with no cached layout_children re-collects regardless: it has
nothing to skip to, and a panic mid-layout would otherwise strand it as
None and resolve the whole page to zero height.

Inline <svg> serializes to usvg at box construction, and SVG-internal
attributes cascade to nothing, so stylo computes no damage and the
snapshot froze. set_attribute now walks to the outermost enclosing <svg>
and stamps CONSTRUCT_BOX.

Inline containers that a measure pass left at max-content, and inlines a
re-collect clobbered, are re-broken against the box the node actually
kept rather than by rebuilding the float context. A rebuilt tree has no
lines and only taffy makes lines, so "no lines" now counts as a
break-width mismatch too. Nodes that registered floats bust their layout
cache.

restore_clobbered_inline_breaks has nothing dirty to key off, so it
runs every resolve. Its inline roots come from an index appended at the
four sites that install inline_layout_data, pruned in the same retain
that performs the width check and sorted only when a push site ran,
instead of a walk over the whole slab. On a 271k-node page only 82.8k
nodes carry inline_layout_data, and hunting for them cost 3.9ms of an
8.1ms layout phase (now 6.4ms). A root escaping the index would
silently never re-break, so a debug_assert re-derives the set the slow
way on every debug resolve.
